^{:go/end 135} (go/method SetBytes "SetBytes sets p to the compressed, uncompressed, or infinity value encoded in\nb, as specified in SEC 1, Version 2.0, Section 2.3.4. If the point is not on\nthe curve, it returns nil and an error, and the receiver is unchanged.\nOtherwise, it returns p.\n" [^{:tag (* P256Point)} p ^{:tag (slice byte)} b] :results [(* P256Point) error]
  ;; This implementation operates in the Montgomery domain with R = 2²⁵⁶ mod
  ;; p. Elements in the Montgomery domain take the form a×R and p256Mul
  ;; calculates (a × b × R⁻¹) mod p. rr is R in the domain, or R×R mod p, thus
  ;; p256Mul(e, RR) gives e×R, i.e. converts e into the Montgomery domain.
